From 22a68b4305894c18fc77507c7ef09112e26a2060 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:30:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wpa_supplicant: stop retrying sched scan on persistent driver
 rejection

hostap 2026-07 drives background station scanning through scheduled
scans whenever the driver advertises max_sched_scan_ssids. On
brcmfmac (AP6275P/BCM43752) every wildcard background-scan attempt is
rejected and wpa_supplicant retries forever, producing an endless
"Failed to initiate sched scan" warning loop, one per scan cycle
(~every 4 s, ~20k lines/day into the persistent system log) whenever
the STA is disconnected and the configured SSID is not visible. Each
attempt falls back to a normal scan, so connectivity keeps working
and only the log is polluted.

brcmfmac implements scheduled scans exclusively as firmware PNO and
rejects requests without match sets (n_match_sets == 0 -> -EINVAL),
which is exactly what the wildcard background scan sends; the nl80211
wrapper also maps pre-send build failures to plain -1, so a specific
errno cannot be relied upon.

Latch the failure: on any sched-scan error other than the transient
-EAGAIN/-EBUSY/-EALREADY, clear wpa_s->max_sched_scan_ssids so that
wpa_supplicant_req_sched_scan() bails out immediately on subsequent
cycles and the background scan loop goes straight to normal scans
without logging. The warning now includes the errno for diagnostics.
Match-set based PNO (control interface) is not used on OpenWrt and
gets disabled as well once the latch triggers.

diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/scan.c b/wpa_supplicant/scan.c
index edd5167..ccf6014 100644
--- a/wpa_supplicant/scan.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/scan.c
@@ -1947,7 +1947,22 @@ scan:
 	os_free(params.filter_ssids);
 	os_free(params.mac_addr);
 	if (ret) {
-		wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_WARNING, "Failed to initiate sched scan");
+		wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_WARNING, "Failed to initiate sched scan: %d", ret);
+		if (ret != -EAGAIN && ret != -EBUSY && ret != -EALREADY) {
+			/*
+			 * The driver rejected a wildcard scheduled scan: e.g.
+			 * brcmfmac implements scheduled scans as firmware PNO
+			 * and requires at least one match set, which background
+			 * scans do not carry. Do not keep retrying scheduled
+			 * scans; the background scan loop falls back to normal
+			 * scans. Transient errors (-EAGAIN/-EBUSY/-EALREADY)
+			 * keep the retry behaviour.
+			 */
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+				   "Driver rejected wildcard sched scan (ret=%d) - disabling sched scan offload",
+				   ret);
+			wpa_s->max_sched_scan_ssids = 0;
+		}
 		if (prev_state != wpa_s->wpa_state)
 			wpa_supplicant_set_state(wpa_s, prev_state);
 		return ret;
-- 
2.50.1

